# The bare fixture repository is committed byte for byte: git never converts
# its line endings and never diffs or merges it as text. Its refs and config
# are text files, but git reads them exactly as written. `binary` is short for
# `-diff -merge -text`.
fixtures/target-repo.git/** binary
# The C2SP CCTV age vectors are vendored byte for byte too. Some hold CRLF line
# endings on purpose (`header_crlf`, `armor_crlf`) and the age file after each
# vector's header is binary, so git must never convert their line endings.
fixtures/cctv-age/** binary
# The common run directory's `capture.bin` is the one fixture that must not be
# UTF-8 text (it holds the byte 0xFF). Marked binary so git never converts its
# bytes or diffs it as text, whatever the checkout's settings.
fixtures/common/capture.bin binary
